## Task Anatomy

```text
<task-id>/
├── task/
│   ├── task.toml
│   ├── instruction.md
│   ├── environment/Dockerfile, repo/, problem_statement.md
│   ├── solution/solve.sh, golden.patch
│   └── tests/test.sh, tests.patch, config.json, grade.py
└── runs/          # reference only — do not upload
```

| Artifact | Compact purpose |
|----------|-----------------|
| `task.toml` | Resources, timeouts, source, category, difficulty explanation |
| `instruction.md` | Agent-facing problem + measurable success criteria |
| `environment/Dockerfile` | Offline-buildable container |
| `environment/repo/` | Base checkout at `base_commit_sha` (HEAD is source of truth) |
| `environment/problem_statement.md` | **Exact copy** of final `instruction.md` |
| `solution/solve.sh` | Applies/produces solved state |
| `solution/golden.patch` | Canonical self-contained solution patch |
| `tests/test.sh` | Runs suite; writes reward; exit matches reward |
| `tests/tests.patch` | Injects new fail-to-pass tests onto base |
| `tests/config.json` | Commands + f2p/p2p test IDs |
| `tests/grade.py` | Grading logic |
| `runs/` | Agent logs for timeouts / misreads / instability |

**Expected relationship:** instruction ↔ tests ↔ oracle must align with each other and the source PR. Tests prove the instruction; oracle proves solvability; environment must support both offline.

